# A tag double battle, BATTLE_TYPE_TAG_DOUBLES, two different enemy
# trainers and no partner.
#
# The fourth variant, TRAINER_WITH_AI_PARTNER, is NOT a station and the
# reason is written here rather than left as a gap: it asks the player to
# pick a TARGET each turn, and a station driven with A alone sits on that
# prompt. Driving it needs a script that knows the target grid's geometry,
# which every other station here avoids on purpose.
name FIGHTER
gender GENDER_MALE
trainer-id 20007
money 15000
badge BADGE_ID_COAL
badge BADGE_ID_FOREST
badge BADGE_ID_COBBLE
party SPECIES_INFERNAPE 40 ITEM_NONE
party SPECIES_STARAPTOR 40 ITEM_NONE
# The lead's first move is set explicitly. A battle station is driven
# with A alone, which picks move slot 0 every turn, so a lead whose
# natural slot 0 is a status move never ends its fight, measured on a
# level 22 Monferno, which drew a level 5 Starly out past 40,000 frames.
party-move 0 0 MOVE_FLAMETHROWER
party-move 1 0 MOVE_BRAVE_BIRD
map MAP_HEADER_HEARTHOME_CITY 0x1D1 0x2BA FACE_DOWN
